#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179521 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179666 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d5ee41f2-7116-52f4-b1f7-923997d994ab" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Double Sum Over a Rectangular Partition Using a Difference of Squares"}] :question/id #uuid "500e1ff1-1a58-57f5-8d85-32ff78dafb35" :question/math-academy-id "e-6117" :question/problem "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- $P_1 = \\left\\{x_0, x_1, \\ldots, x_m\\right\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[4, 6]$\n\n- $P_2 = \\left\\{y_0, y_1, \\ldots, y_n\\right\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[2, 6]$\n\nCalculate  $\\displaystyle\\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n (x_i + x_{i-1})\\Delta x_i \\Delta y_j,$ where $\\Delta x_i = x_i - x_{i-1}$ and $\\Delta y_j = y_j - y_{j-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the product rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^m (x_i + x_{i-1})\\Delta x_i \\cdot \\sum_{j=1}^n \\Delta y_j.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^n\\Delta y_j$ is just the length of the interval $[2, 6].$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=6-2=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the sum over $i,$ we can evaluate it as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})Δ{x}_{1}+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})Δ{x}_{2}+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})Δ{x}_{m} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}\\,+\\,{x}_{0})({x}_{1}\\,-\\,{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}\\,+\\,{x}_{1})({x}_{2}\\,-\\,{x}_{1})+({x}_{m}\\,+\\,{x}_{m-1})({x}_{m}\\,-\\,{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})+({x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{m-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}}-{x}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}^{2}+{x}_{m}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={6}^{2}-{4}^{2} \\\\  & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we finally arrive at \n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^m (x_i + x_{i-1})\\Delta x_i \\cdot \\sum_{j=1}^n\\Delta y_j = 20\\cdot 4 = 80.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179584 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179722 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f913fab-d0b5-5e9e-b292-039afe4a148c" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Double Sum Over a Rectangular Partition"}] :question/id #uuid "e2f01953-2fb1-5ddb-83ae-5d8a73e7f7ac" :question/math-academy-id "e-9482" :question/problem "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- $P_1 = \\left\\{x_0, x_1, \\ldots, x_m\\right\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[-1, 2]$\n\n- $P_2 = \\left\\{y_0, y_1, \\ldots, y_n\\right\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[2, 3]$\n\nCalculate $\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n {3} \\Delta x_i \\Delta y_j,$ where $\\Delta x_i = x_i - x_{i-1}$ and $\\Delta y_j = y_j - y_{j-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple and product rules, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}3Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & =3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^m\\Delta x_i$ and $\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^n\\Delta y_j$ are just the lengths of the intervals $[-1, 2]$ and $[2,3]$ respectively. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i} & =2-(-1)=3, \\\\ {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j} & =3-2=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we have\n\n$$\n3 \\sum_{i=1}^m \\Delta x_i \\sum_{j=1}^n \\Delta y_j = 3 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 1 = 9.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179979 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179722 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f913fab-d0b5-5e9e-b292-039afe4a148c" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Double Sum Over a Rectangular Partition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43466d22-8b48-55a6-bf28-957026cac2ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254244} {:answer/id #uuid "55b18526-955c-50d0-b566-01dce50dca98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254419} {:answer/id #uuid "57c1775a-dfcb-570e-be88-c4c7df1d41a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254442} {:answer/id #uuid "a4e273af-9b7d-518f-9227-01b071590528" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255125} {:answer/id #uuid "b638c667-208e-545f-9953-26e2b3c9f50c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255282}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4e273af-9b7d-518f-9227-01b071590528" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255125} :answer-field/id #uuid "192e1cce-6291-501b-a0bd-b0d1f2458310" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255963}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7cb18f0a-5793-5799-850f-ef66cbf9de18" :question/math-academy-id "q-122867" :question/problem "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- ${P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}}$ is a partition of the interval $[0,2]$\n\n- ${P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}}$ is a partition of the interval $[1,6]$\n\nCalculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j},$ where $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the product rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}$ and ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}$ are just the lengths of the intervals $[0,2]$ and $[1,6]$ respectively. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i} & =2-0=2, \\\\ {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j} & =6-1=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we have\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=2\\cdot 5=10.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275216 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179722 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f913fab-d0b5-5e9e-b292-039afe4a148c" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Double Sum Over a Rectangular Partition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "764f2946-f8f8-5227-89df-c89e81610b47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273394} {:answer/id #uuid "78dffdf3-b4b8-5a5c-b180-4d8021ba070d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273422} {:answer/id #uuid "aff5fee7-0ee1-5c19-99a6-116ab9cf7dfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273910} {:answer/id #uuid "c78f5abc-91a5-5d22-90f0-86f9268bdd7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274123} {:answer/id #uuid "df8a276c-dfc4-5935-b89d-f9fbf1bb8487" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274360}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78dffdf3-b4b8-5a5c-b180-4d8021ba070d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273422} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d718573-0055-5ccf-8a08-cae2d3f001ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274820}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ba5f3cf2-5db7-5ec1-b7c9-a70950beee5d" :question/math-academy-id "q-149628" :question/problem "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- ${P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}}$ is a partition of the interval $[2,3]$\n\n- ${P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}}$ is a partition of the interval $[3,8]$\n\nCalculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}4Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j},$ where $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple and product rules, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}4Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =4{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & =4{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}$ and ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}$ are just the lengths of the intervals $[2,3]$ and $[3,8]$ respectively. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i} & =3-2=1, \\\\ {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j} & =8-3=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we have\n\n$$\n4{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=4\\cdot 1\\cdot 5=20.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275218 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179666 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d5ee41f2-7116-52f4-b1f7-923997d994ab" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Double Sum Over a Rectangular Partition Using a Difference of Squares"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f1eeb58-a136-5d3c-84f2-2d63eda0900c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272806} {:answer/id #uuid "45cf60ce-5115-565e-8a96-7b643ba4957e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272985} {:answer/id #uuid "9bcbf429-aa17-52aa-bd18-07ddfa5bf720" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273738} {:answer/id #uuid "c0fd64d0-c112-5c74-9369-9bc7fd6b6f83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274064} {:answer/id #uuid "f1550d82-2633-5abb-9927-288d0904b5b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274523}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45cf60ce-5115-565e-8a96-7b643ba4957e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272985} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4f7deb4-d91c-5fde-bcfe-1de4ed02beac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274949}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "05d90303-b25e-5d42-93e9-d95362fdcd2f" :question/math-academy-id "q-149631" :question/problem "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- ${P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}}$ is a partition of the interval $[3,5]$\n\n- ${P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}}$ is a partition of the interval $[-1,2]$\n\nCalculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j},$ where $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the product rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}$ is just the length of the interval $[3,5].$ So, we have\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}=5-3=2.\n$$\n\nFor the sum over $j,$ we evaluate it as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j} & =({y}_{1}+{y}_{0})Δ{y}_{1}+({y}_{2}+{y}_{1})Δ{y}_{2}+⋯+({y}_{n}+{x}_{n-1})Δ{y}_{n} \\\\  & =({y}_{1}+{y}_{0})({y}_{1}-{y}_{0})+({y}_{2}+{y}_{1})({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})+⋯+({y}_{n}+{x}_{n-1})({y}_{n}-{y}_{n-1}) \\\\  & =({y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{0}^{2})+({y}_{2}^{2}-{y}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({y}_{n}^{2}-{y}_{n-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{y}_{1}^{2}}-{y}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{y}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{y}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({y}_{n}^{2}-\\cancel{{y}_{n-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{y}_{0}^{2}+{y}_{n}^{2} \\\\  & ={y}_{n}^{2}-{y}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={2}^{2}-(-1)^{2} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we finally arrive at \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j}=2\\cdot 3=6.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180268 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179666 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d5ee41f2-7116-52f4-b1f7-923997d994ab" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Double Sum Over a Rectangular Partition Using a Difference of Squares"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95d34ba7-f70e-5bde-a60f-f0c96ad96341" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179153} {:answer/id #uuid "c56bbebc-c48f-5c5c-b940-c2f97f2af460" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179154} {:answer/id #uuid "e8802437-9f26-5e47-b836-a50a564ead55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179155} {:answer/id #uuid "0c1ec69d-8237-53ab-b125-deba7bb578fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179156} {:answer/id #uuid "31e69d82-7c37-5b8c-a0a6-d027fcca6a8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179157}] :answer-field/id #uuid "376d3cb3-e1a1-527b-b302-47ad3abeeb22" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179152}] :question/id #uuid "a88af1ba-c0a1-5207-b3ae-5df258155f41" :question/math-academy-id "q-72129" :question/problem "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- $P_{1} = {x_{0}, x_{1}, …, x_{m}}$ is a partition of the interval $[2, 5]$\n- $P_{2} = {y_{0}, y_{1}, …, y_{n}}$ is a partition of the interval $[0, 2]$\n\nCalculate $∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)(y_{j} + y_{j - 1})Δx_{i}Δy_{j}$, where $Δx_{i} = x_{i} - x_{i - 1}$ and $Δy_{j} = y_{j} - y_{j - 1}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339124 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179722 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f913fab-d0b5-5e9e-b292-039afe4a148c" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Double Sum Over a Rectangular Partition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f340918-7d6f-57a3-802c-2a1453e19f4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336176} {:answer/id #uuid "1e6713dd-9c1e-5e34-9885-5b2724869b1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336312} {:answer/id #uuid "23b4bd72-02b7-51b2-b68b-faa59bb1d133" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336368} {:answer/id #uuid "7f353096-d48c-53d2-aa18-aad41c76beaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337186} {:answer/id #uuid "ed6bd1da-b395-52c6-a69f-b695cbeea7dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338103}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f353096-d48c-53d2-aa18-aad41c76beaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337186} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc552339-f759-5a74-96f9-f40e0ccdedae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338616}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9f73aa4c-df24-5091-bd74-35aefea94a85" :question/math-academy-id "q-72476" :question/problem "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- ${P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}}$ is a partition of the interval $[0,1]$\n\n- ${P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}}$ is a partition of the interval $[1,2]$\n\nCalculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}3Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j},$ where $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple and product rules, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}3Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & =3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}$ and ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}$ are just the lengths of the intervals $[0,1]$ and $[1,2]$ respectively. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i} & =1-0=1, \\\\ {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j} & =2-1=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we have \n\n$$\n3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=3\\cdot 1\\cdot 1=3.\n$$"}]}
